{
 "_about": "The weights engine's data (see brain/weights.py and docs/culture.md). Each area is one decision with a few options. An option's score = bias + sum(affinity x (slider + the fort's leanings) / 100) + sum(history weight x count, capped). Affinities run from -1 to +1 (a little more for a slider's main option). Quirks add bonuses to options and can change how sticky choices are. Tune freely: tests/test_weights.py checks every option can still be reached and that opposite sliders choose differently. (0.95) At default sliders the top two options of each area sit within the close-call band (near), so the fort's seed and its own and its site's leanings (brain/leanings.py) decide.",
